WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.199
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book three.

2
00:00:05.499 --> 00:00:08.828
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.128 --> 00:00:15.054
Unit eleven: Natural Disasters. Today you will imagine situations with the second conditional.

4
00:00:15.354 --> 00:00:17.902
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.867 --> 00:00:22.308
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:24.070
Earthquake.

7
00:00:25.083 --> 00:00:27.640
Earthquake means a sudden shaking of the ground.

8
00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:30.505
The earthquake damaged many buildings.

9
00:00:31.117 --> 00:00:34.384
Your turn. Say: Earthquake.

10
00:00:37.233 --> 00:00:38.246
Earthquake.

11
00:00:38.983 --> 00:00:39.822
Flood.

12
00:00:40.817 --> 00:00:43.339
Flood means a lot of water covering dry land.

13
00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:45.996
The flood covered the rice fields.

14
00:00:46.583 --> 00:00:49.189
Your turn. Say: Flood.

15
00:00:52.033 --> 00:00:52.767
Flood.

16
00:00:53.517 --> 00:00:54.785
Evacuation.

17
00:00:55.783 --> 00:00:58.979
Evacuation means moving people away from danger.

18
00:00:59.583 --> 00:01:01.502
The evacuation began at night.

19
00:01:02.117 --> 00:01:04.943
Your turn. Say: Evacuation.

20
00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:09.068
Evacuation.

21
00:01:09.817 --> 00:01:10.911
Preparedness.

22
00:01:11.917 --> 00:01:14.439
Preparedness means being ready for an emergency.

23
00:01:15.050 --> 00:01:17.003
Preparedness saves lives.

24
00:01:17.617 --> 00:01:20.327
Your turn. Say: Preparedness.

25
00:01:23.167 --> 00:01:24.388
Preparedness.

26
00:01:25.150 --> 00:01:26.604
Emergency kit.

27
00:01:27.617 --> 00:01:31.160
Emergency kit means a bag of things you need in a disaster.

28
00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:34.435
Our emergency kit has water and a torch.

29
00:01:35.050 --> 00:01:38.051
Your turn. Say: Emergency kit.

30
00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:42.203
Emergency kit.

31
00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:43.858
Shelter.

32
00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:47.000
Shelter means a safe place to stay.

33
00:01:47.617 --> 00:01:49.303
The school became a shelter.

34
00:01:49.917 --> 00:01:52.418
Your turn. Say: Shelter.

35
00:01:55.267 --> 00:01:56.221
Shelter.

36
00:01:56.983 --> 00:01:58.193
Alert system.

37
00:01:59.183 --> 00:02:02.147
Alert system means a way to warn people quickly.

38
00:02:02.750 --> 00:02:05.202
The alert system sent text messages.

39
00:02:05.817 --> 00:02:08.283
Your turn. Say: Alert system.

40
00:02:11.133 --> 00:02:12.576
Alert system.

41
00:02:13.317 --> 00:02:14.213
Damage.

42
00:02:15.217 --> 00:02:17.576
Damage means harm to things or places.

43
00:02:18.183 --> 00:02:20.078
The storm caused a lot of damage.

44
00:02:20.683 --> 00:02:23.092
Your turn. Say: Damage.

45
00:02:25.933 --> 00:02:26.888
Damage.

46
00:02:27.650 --> 00:02:28.907
Relief effort.

47
00:02:29.917 --> 00:02:33.135
Relief effort means work to help people after a disaster.

48
00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:35.703
Students joined the relief effort.

49
00:02:36.317 --> 00:02:38.876
Your turn. Say: Relief effort.

50
00:02:41.733 --> 00:02:43.036
Relief effort.

51
00:02:43.783 --> 00:02:44.784
Rebuild.

52
00:02:45.783 --> 00:02:48.143
Rebuild means to build again after damage.

53
00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:50.506
The village rebuilt the bridge.

54
00:02:51.117 --> 00:02:53.839
Your turn. Say: Rebuild.

55
00:02:56.700 --> 00:02:57.666
Rebuild.

56
00:02:58.417 --> 00:02:59.487
Resilience.

57
00:03:00.483 --> 00:03:04.039
Resilience means the ability to recover from difficulty.

58
00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:07.044
The community showed great resilience.

59
00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:10.407
Your turn. Say: Resilience.

60
00:03:13.267 --> 00:03:14.419
Resilience.

61
00:03:15.183 --> 00:03:16.150
Survival.

62
00:03:17.150 --> 00:03:20.438
Survival means staying alive in a dangerous situation.

63
00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:23.015
Clean water is key to survival.

64
00:03:23.617 --> 00:03:26.281
Your turn. Say: Survival.

65
00:03:29.133 --> 00:03:30.251
Survival.

66
00:03:31.067 --> 00:03:34.311
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:37.974
Visal, what would you do if a flood happened here?

68
00:03:39.083 --> 00:03:42.511
If a flood happened, we would evacuate immediately.

69
00:03:43.617 --> 00:03:44.653
Where would you go?

70
00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:48.435
We would go to the shelter at the pagoda on the hill.

71
00:03:49.550 --> 00:03:51.364
Do you have an emergency kit?

72
00:03:52.450 --> 00:03:58.007
Yes. If we didn't have one, we would be in danger. Preparedness is important.

73
00:03:59.167 --> 00:04:00.795
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:01.650 --> 00:04:04.172
Grammar focus: Second conditional.

75
00:04:04.472 --> 00:04:05.670
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:06.383 --> 00:04:09.567
If a flood happened, we would evacuate immediately.

77
00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:13.760
If I had an emergency kit, I would feel safer.

78
00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:16.731
What would you do if there was an earthquake?

79
00:04:17.667 --> 00:04:21.860
Use the second conditional for imagined or unlikely situations.

80
00:04:22.617 --> 00:04:26.534
Be careful! Don't say: If a flood happens, we would evacuate.

81
00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:32.183
Say: If a flood happened, we would evacuate.

82
00:04:32.483 --> 00:04:35.562
The second conditional uses the past simple after 'if'.

83
00:04:36.367 --> 00:04:39.019
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:39.833 --> 00:04:41.101
Ready for the Flood.

85
00:04:41.401 --> 00:04:44.620
During the flood, the alert system helped with evacuation.

86
00:04:45.633 --> 00:04:47.900
Families moved to a shelter in the school.

87
00:04:48.900 --> 00:04:52.722
Preparedness and an emergency kit made a big difference for our survival.

88
00:04:53.733 --> 00:04:56.975
After the flood, the relief effort helped us rebuild the damage.

89
00:04:57.967 --> 00:05:01.232
If another flood happened, our resilience would help us again.

90
00:05:02.333 --> 00:05:06.173
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:07.017 --> 00:05:09.806
If a flood happened, we blank evacuate.

92
00:05:10.106 --> 00:05:13.109
A, would. B, will. C, are.

93
00:05:16.667 --> 00:05:18.422
The answer is A: would.

94
00:05:19.583 --> 00:05:22.129
Moving people away from danger is blank.

95
00:05:22.429 --> 00:05:26.105
A, evacuation. B, damage. C, survival.

96
00:05:29.667 --> 00:05:32.479
The answer is A: evacuation.

97
00:05:33.617 --> 00:05:36.522
The ability to recover from difficulty is blank.

98
00:05:36.822 --> 00:05:40.800
A, resilience. B, preparedness. C, shelter.

99
00:05:44.367 --> 00:05:46.889
The answer is A: resilience.

100
00:05:48.100 --> 00:05:51.170
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:05:52.017 --> 00:05:55.026
How can communities prepare for natural disasters?

102
00:06:03.817 --> 00:06:05.271
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:05.571 --> 00:06:14.957
Communities can make an alert system and prepare emergency kits. If a disaster happened, everyone would know where the shelter is.

104
00:06:15.257 --> 00:06:17.430
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:18.317 --> 00:06:22.664
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and second conditional.

106
00:06:22.964 --> 00:06:27.706
Today's value is preparedness. Get ready before an emergency happens.

107
00:06:28.006 --> 00:06:30.763
See you in Unit twelve. Goodbye!

108
00:06:31.063 --> 00:06:34.110
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

